"smart_blocks:Computer Science/JavaScript/JavaScript XMLHttpRequest (Legacy).md#BBFABBA6;\">built-in browser object that provides a way to make HTTP requests to a web server. It allows a web page to request data from the server after the page has loaded, without having to reload the entire page. Despite its name, XHR can work with any type of data, not just XML (e.g., JSON, plain text, HTML).</mark>": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06942793,0.02741255,-0.03646256,0.00703707,-0.03743201,-0.01238434,-0.05858083,-0.02827414,-0.03349279,0.00739558,0.01144346,0.02231375,-0.01986793,0.10729939,0.0055529,0.06653997,-0.00879435,0.00120073,-0.0759293,0.03651296,0.05833566,0.01989567,0.0182309,-0.05256582,-0.02013925,0.00839134,0.01502511,-0.01990237,-0.06143898,-0.13777418,0.02396405,-0.09082194,-0.00217644,-0.05365994,-0.03603888,-0.05766778,0.01142713,-0.04361753,-0.02864679,0.0401663,0.03589844,0.03905402,-0.04254398,-0.01599122,-0.03757644,-0.04414515,-0.02082313,0.00680712,-0.02310961,-0.01031572,-0.03062267,0.01601368,0.09113466,-0.00317615,0.07990698,0.04126317,0.04735746,0.09691188,0.04082108,0.00960731,0.00946577,0.00228368,-0.08359897,0.1290815,0.05104675,0.03329038,-0.05377886,-0.03426709,0.00440352,0.01025426,-0.02160935,0.03449038,-0.01187418,0.08950576,-0.02342121,-0.02726814,0.03797695,-0.0196623,0.01312583,0.02341235,-0.08479695,-0.04661857,0.00372108,0.00047116,0.01043247,-0.01638176,0.02348242,-0.04556679,0.06877036,0.04950847,-0.05548246,-0.03078517,-0.07282992,-0.01403923,-0.03993174,0.00080248,-0.00721369,0.04619165,-0.03216504,0.10232499,-0.00630011,0.02933581,0.02504472,-0.0471329,0.02523747,-0.04708005,-0.03793737,-0.04315335,-0.04918333,0.00142248,-0.01713168,-0.04701065,-0.04549756,-0.04300288,-0.06418517,0.05238628,-0.06163275,0.02723976,-0.02284095,-0.07901271,0.05288703,0.00267662,0.04622222,0.00160737,0.0398208,0.00608062,0.03588779,0.06720061,-0.03583125,0.06730123,0.04674876,-0.02243433,-0.07332391,-0.0079738,-0.